## Scope of this licence

This licence covers the **catalogue content** (Markdown source under
`taxonomy/`, the assembled `avt-metrics-taxonomy.md`, the rendered MkDocs
site, and the supporting cross-cutting documents at the repo root such as
`plan-future.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and `README.md`).

The licence does **not** cover:

- **Quoted framework material** — references to DTAC, NHS England IG
  Guidance, MHRA SaMD documents, Caldicott Principles, NICE ESF, NHS
  T.E.S.T., DSPT, FHIR UK Core, PRSB, UK GDPR, the FTS notice 069369-2025,
  and other external sources cited in the catalogue. Each remains under its
  publisher's own licence; the catalogue cites them under fair-dealing /
  fair-use conventions for review and commentary.
- **Code in `pkg/`** — the `avt-metrics-ref` reference implementation
  package is licensed separately under MIT (see `pkg/avt_metrics_ref/LICENSE`).
- **Code in `taxonomy/`** — the build / parse / audit / site-build Python
  source in `taxonomy/build.py`, `taxonomy/parse.py`, `taxonomy/audit.py`,
  `taxonomy/build_site.py`, the `taxonomy/tools/` and `taxonomy/tests/`
  directories. This tooling is supplied to make the catalogue reproducible;
  if you re-use it independently of the catalogue content, treat it as MIT
  licensed for that purpose.

If you have a use case that doesn't fit cleanly into these categories,
open an issue at https://github.com/danjscho/avt-metrics-taxonomy/issues
and we'll figure it out.
